{
    "background_story": "Lucca was a well-respected elder in his small Italian village. He had a paternalistic nature, always looking out for the well-being of those around him. Lucca took it upon himself to guide the younger generations, sharing his wisdom and life experiences to help them navigate the complexities of adulthood. He would often invite the village children to his workshop, teaching them traditional craftsmanship and the value of hard work. Lucca's kind but firm demeanor earned him the nickname 'Il Padre' (The Father) among the villagers. He would offer advice and assistance to those in need, sometimes to the point of being overbearing, but always with the best intentions. Lucca's paternalistic nature had a profound impact on the community, creating a sense of unity and responsibility among its members.",
